<title>FRANCE: HORSE RACING-GRAND PRIX DE PARIS RESULT.</title>
<headline>HORSE RACING-GRAND PRIX DE PARIS RESULT.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-06-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Result of the group one Grand Prix</p>
<p>de Paris horse race, for three-year-olds, run over 10 furlongs</p>
<p>(2-km) at Longchamp on Sunday:</p>
<p>1. Peintre Celebre (ridden by Olivier Peslier)</p>
<p>2. Ithaki (Cash Asmussen)</p>
<p>3. Shaka (Jean-Rene Dubosc)</p>
<p>4. Alekos (Dominique Boeuf)</p>
<p>7 ran. Distances: Two lengths, one length, five lengths.</p>
<p>Winner owned by Daniel Wildenstein, trained by Andre Fabre in</p>
<p>France. Value to the winner: $226,262.</p>
<p>Pari-Mutuel (includes a one-franc stake): Win 1.40 (coupled</p>
<p>with Super Cub); places 1.10, 2.10. Straight Forecast 8.10.</p>
</text>
